# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore  -  RetailAPOLLO
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the repo had none, which is the reason six
# __pycache__ directories, a .pytest_cache and twelve LaTeX intermediates
# had accumulated and needed a manual sweep.  Deleting them once fixes the
# symptom; ignoring them fixes the cause.
#
# RULE OF THUMB used below: ignore anything a COMMAND can regenerate from
# committed inputs, and never ignore anything a command cannot.  That is why
# ABSTRACTED_DATA/ is absent from this file - it is the committed, text-free
# transfer folder (src/abstracted_data.py export/hydrate), i.e. an INPUT on a
# fresh machine, not an artefact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Python bytecode / tooling caches (regenerated on next run) ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- virtual environments ----
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- LaTeX intermediates -------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by `pdflatex` on every compile.  The .pdf is NOT ignored: the
# deck is a deliverable and a reader without a TeX install still needs it.
*.aux
*.log
*.nav
*.out
*.snm
*.toc
*.vrb
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.bbl
*.blg

# ---- raw / private data --------------------------------------------------
# The raw store holds post TEXT and author handles, so it must never be
# committed.  data/processed/ is derived (rebuildable from a hydrate) and
# large, so it stays local too; ABSTRACTED_DATA/ is the committed form.
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/cache/
logs/

# ---- OS noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- machine-local pipeline ledgers (2026-07-27) -------------------------
# These two files MEASURE THIS MACHINE: how long each stage takes here, and
# what each subreddit costs when crawled from here.  Committing them would
# plan the laptop's run with the desktop's numbers - a slower machine would
# inherit a page allowance it cannot afford inside the desk's ~10-minute
# ceiling, and quietly overrun on every run.  Each falls back to a measured
# bootstrap prior in src/config.py and re-measures itself within one run, so
# a fresh clone loses nothing but one run's worth of precision.
# See src/pipeline_budget.py.
data/reference/pipeline_stage_times.json
data/reference/reddit_comments_cost.json

# Backfill progress ledger (tools/backfill_reddit.py): which historical
# chunks THIS machine has already pulled. Local operational state - the
# data it describes lands in data/raw, which is never committed either.
data/reference/reddit_backfill_progress.json

# AI layer: local-only text + operational state (never committed - the
# same text-free boundary as data/raw)
data/reference/agentic_samples.jsonl
data/reference/agentic_scan_ledger.json
data/reference/nb10_sample_texts.jsonl

# ---- .env IS TRACKED ON PURPOSE ----
# Desk decision 2026-08-06: ".env to be committed in the future, its
# fine." So it is NOT ignored, and the credentials it holds travel with
# the repository.
#
# Two things follow from that, neither of them optional:
#   * this repo must stay private. Anyone with read access has the
#     FetchLayer key and the Apollo gateway password.
#   * rotating a key means committing the rotation, so the OLD value
#     stays in history forever. Treat every key that has ever been in
#     here as burned the day the repo leaves the desk.
#
# POST_INTERN_HANDOVER.md previously claimed this file was git-ignored.
# It never was - the only matching pattern was `env/`, the virtualenv
# DIRECTORY, which never matched a file called `.env`. The claim is
# corrected there.

# ---- new_ice_data/ : A VENDOR DELIVERY UNDER EVALUATION ----
# Desk instruction 2026-08-20: "make sure this whole thing dosnt get
# commited". Ignored for two reasons, and the second matters more than
# the first:
#
#   1. SIZE. The delivery is a 2.6 GB zip plus a 2.8 GB split archive
#      unpacked beside it. Nothing that large belongs in git history,
#      where it can never be truly deleted.
#   2. RAW TEXT. It is unaggregated Reddit posts. This project's
#      standing rule is that only TEXT-FREE aggregates are committable
#      (see ABSTRACTED_DATA and the verify_abstracted safety check in
#      update_data.py) - raw post text is precisely what must never
#      reach the repository. A vendor sample is no exception.
#
# The notebook that evaluates the delivery IS tracked (it is code, and
# it is how the assessment is reproduced); everything it reads and
# everything it writes is not.
# Both spellings are listed on purpose. The folder on the desk machine
# is "New_ICE_data"; gitignore matching follows core.ignorecase, which
# is true on Windows and FALSE on Linux, so a single lowercase rule
# would silently stop protecting this folder the day the repo is cloned
# anywhere else. Two rules cost nothing and cannot fail that way.
new_ice_data/*
!new_ice_data/explore_ice_source.py
!new_ice_data/explore_ice_source.ipynb
New_ICE_data/*
!New_ICE_data/explore_ice_source.py
!New_ICE_data/explore_ice_source.ipynb
